  "prompt": "What standard deduction is allowed in computing the net estate?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nIn computing the net estate, the standard deduction allowed is based on the provisions of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), specifically under Section 86, which provides for a standard deduction of P5,000,000 for the estate of a decedent.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe standard deduction of P5,000,000 is applicable to the gross estate of a decedent, which reduces the taxable estate before calculating the estate tax. This deduction is intended to simplify the computation of the net estate and provide relief to the heirs.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estate planning and tax purposes, the standard deduction significantly lowers the taxable amount of the estate, potentially reducing the estate tax liability. Executors and heirs should be aware of this deduction when preparing the estate tax return to ensure compliance and optimize tax outcomes.",
